DISTRIBUTION-ONLY: its subject is a tree built by running scripts/install.sh into an empty
directory, and install.sh is not shipped to consumers. On a consumer this fixture cannot resolve
its installer and would exit 2 on every run.

It is also a MUTATION BATTERY: it edits copies of five installed core scripts
(sprint-status.sh, sync-taught-schema.sh, validate-audit-anchors.sh,
validate-write-format-steering.sh, validate-gate-adjudication.sh) inside whole-tree copies of
that install. The distribution-side half of the same property — each script consults its root
before its install fallback — reaches consumers through validator-path-resolution, which ships.

It also carries the distribution-only arms of two SHIPPING fixtures, which cannot declare
scripts/install.sh or templates/ (absent on a consumer, so exit 2): layer-crosswalk-home's
installer scaffold/preserve arms (CW1/CW2) and handoff-completion-assertion's e6-order
template check and its control (HO1/HO2).
